1124|n|A kind of deep blue, one of the seven prismatic colors. ; A blue dyestuff obtained from several plants belonging to very different genera and orders; as, the woad, Isatis tinctoria, Indigofera tinctoria, I. Anil, Nereum tinctorium, etc. It is a dark blue earthy substance, tasteless and odorless, with a copper-violet luster when rubbed. Indigo does not exist in the plants as such, but is obtained by decomposition of the glycoside indican.	n:1asr,96,2;mxv,60,3;273t,9,2~mxv,60,3;1asr,96,2;273t,9,2	N:1jdr,104,1;15jf,91,3~15jf,91,3;1jdr,104,1
1124|v|A kind of deep blue, one of the seven prismatic colors. ; A blue dyestuff obtained from several plants belonging to very different genera and orders; as, the woad, Isatis tinctoria, Indigofera tinctoria, I. Anil, Nereum tinctorium, etc. It is a dark blue earthy substance, tasteless and odorless, with a copper-violet luster when rubbed. Indigo does not exist in the plants as such, but is obtained by decomposition of the glycoside indican.	o:mxv,44,1~mxv,44,1
